{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"936ac7541000db4f9937d8d733cb19c5ace817ec9d77ac25d857825b88329351","digest":{"component_or_area":"LLM Bedrock provider region resolution","key_entities":["build_bedrock_provider","resolve_bedrock_region","src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py","src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py","provenance_for","boto3.session.Session","REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION","AWS_DEFAULT_REGION","AWS_REGION","region_name","region_source","LLMConfigError"],"problem_keywords":["bedrock region resolution","AWS_REGION environment variable","region configuration precedence","bedrock provider initialization"],"propositions":["Bedrock LLM operations fail when only AWS_REGION environment variable is set, because botocore does not consult it and rebar passes no explicit region to boto3.Session","Resolution order must be: REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION (config) > AWS_DEFAULT_REGION (env) > AWS_REGION (env) > boto3 profile ambient fallback","A pure resolve_bedrock_region function must return (region, source) tuple and be called by build_bedrock_provider to pass region_name explicitly to boto3.Session, bypassing botocore's limitation","Provider provenance must record region and region_source fields for bedrock runs when rebar's resolution chain succeeds, and omit them when only boto3 profile resolution applies"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1786756211603625001,"uuid":"b906ed4a-a134-421f-b570-b856c7703140"}